00:30:55,160 --> 00:30:56,100
Look at you.

274
00:30:57,790 --> 00:31:00,290
You're so pale.

275
00:31:00,360 --> 00:31:05,290
You haven't been eating much for days and you look so pale now...

276
00:31:11,290 --> 00:31:13,290
Is something stressing you out, sweetie?

277
00:31:28,700 --> 00:31:29,520
It’s okay.

278
00:31:30,090 --> 00:31:32,090
If you don't want to tell me, you don't have to.

279
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:35,300
But don't forget to eat, alright?

280
00:31:38,640 --> 00:31:40,640
Don't cry now.

281
00:31:42,420 --> 00:31:43,880
Don't cry, sweetie.

282
00:31:47,980 --> 00:31:49,240
Eat up, okay?

283
00:31:50,170 --> 00:31:51,260
I'll leave you now.

284
00:33:22,610 --> 00:33:24,490
Hello, hello.

285
00:33:25,020 --> 00:33:27,290
All three of you are here together. Is there something you need?

286
00:33:27,580 --> 00:33:28,450
Is Kaew here?

287
00:33:28,870 --> 00:33:30,060
She is. She's upstairs.

288
00:33:30,100 --> 00:33:30,770
Let me go up and call her for you.

289
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:31,550
No need, thanks.

290
00:33:50,530 --> 00:33:52,530
Why did you come here?

291
00:33:54,090 --> 00:33:55,380
Ouch! Ouch!

292
00:34:01,380 --> 00:34:02,170
What the hell are you doing to me?

293
00:34:02,220 --> 00:34:03,090
It hurts!

294
00:34:03,260 --> 00:34:04,400
It's good that it hurts.

295
00:34:06,100 --> 00:34:07,140
You're getting exactly what you deserve!

296
00:34:07,740 --> 00:34:09,139
Kie!

297
00:34:12,030 --> 00:34:13,040
What the fuck...

298
00:34:18,150 --> 00:34:19,880
Aww!

299
00:34:21,880 --> 00:34:23,880
Are you crazy? It hurts!

300
00:34:30,580 --> 00:34:31,580
Was this you?

301
00:34:33,650 --> 00:34:35,409
How dare you call someone else shameless,

302
00:34:36,159 --> 00:34:37,850
when you're even more shameless yourself?

303
00:34:40,610 --> 00:34:41,719
Are you in shock?

304
00:34:42,320 --> 00:34:44,510
How could you do this to me, you bitch Kaew?

305
00:34:47,520 --> 00:34:49,840
Do you think I'm that stupid, huh?

306
00:34:53,260 --> 00:34:57,139
We've been friends since we were kids,

307
00:34:58,640 --> 00:35:01,560
how could you do this to me, huh? Kaew?

308
00:35:01,710 --> 00:35:03,620
How could you do this to me?

309
00:35:03,680 --> 00:35:06,310
Kie! Let me go!

310
00:35:12,990 --> 00:35:14,140
A friend?

311
00:35:14,630 --> 00:35:16,630
Do you call someone like you a friend?

312
00:35:17,430 --> 00:35:20,020
Why? Is it because I'm poorer,

313
00:35:20,270 --> 00:35:22,970
so you keep putting me down, bossing me around,

314
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:24,970
and treating me like your lackey?

315
00:35:26,970 --> 00:35:29,850
"Kaew, do my homework for me."

316
00:35:30,310 --> 00:35:33,270
"Kaew, go save a table for me."

317
00:35:35,030 --> 00:35:37,450
You've always just looked at me like a dog.

318
00:35:39,790 --> 00:35:40,570
What,

319
00:35:41,440 --> 00:35:47,480
can't you handle the fact that today a dog like me beat you?

320
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:49,450
Do you actually believe what she's saying?

321
00:35:50,180 --> 00:35:51,850
Aren't you being too full of yourself?

322
00:35:52,910 --> 00:35:53,870
Fake an orgasm,

323
00:35:54,790 --> 00:35:56,330
she probably didn't say that just to you.

324
00:35:57,850 --> 00:35:58,760
Kie!

325
00:36:03,690 --> 00:36:07,490
Someone like you who would even steal a friend's wife.

326
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:09,510
What right do you have to slap me?

327
00:36:09,830 --> 00:36:10,870
Why wouldn't I have the right?

328
00:36:12,150 --> 00:36:14,050
Pha and I were together before you even showed up!

329
00:36:14,920 --> 00:36:18,560
The one who stole Pha away was you, not me.

330
00:36:23,360 --> 00:36:27,590
That's not true! If you two were together first,

331
00:36:28,980 --> 00:36:30,360
why would Pha marry me?

332
00:36:30,400 --> 00:36:32,360
Why did she marry you?

333
00:36:33,610 --> 00:36:35,100
Because of money! Because you're rich!

334
00:36:35,620 --> 00:36:37,030
I just let Pha sleep with you

335
00:36:37,080 --> 00:36:39,030
so she could take your money

336
00:36:40,030 --> 00:36:44,090
and bring it back to me.

337
00:36:48,020 --> 00:36:49,510
You really are an idiot, aren't you?

338
00:36:49,890 --> 00:36:50,790
What are you laughing at?

339
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:52,100
Have you gone mad?!

340
00:36:54,710 --> 00:36:58,030
Pha and I never registered our marriage,

341
00:36:59,180 --> 00:37:00,610
didn't she tell you?

342
00:37:03,700 --> 00:37:04,990
You stupid bitch.

343
00:37:05,720 --> 00:37:09,510
No matter how badly you want my fortune, you can't have it.

344
00:37:11,190 --> 00:37:12,730
I won’t register a marriage with anyone at all.

345
00:37:14,880 --> 00:37:17,450
You got played for free

346
00:37:19,080 --> 00:37:20,740
and then scammed out of my money.

347
00:37:21,530 --> 00:37:23,420
You are seriously stupid over and over again.

348
00:37:23,460 --> 00:37:24,140
Kie!

349
00:37:41,890 --> 00:37:44,160
That's enough, P'Kie. That's enough.

350
00:37:44,960 --> 00:37:47,600
Kaew Kaew!

351
00:37:47,860 --> 00:37:49,190
A bullshit friend like her

352
00:37:50,390 --> 00:37:51,770
deserves this.

353
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:53,330
Kie, stop it.

354
00:37:55,730 --> 00:37:56,340
Let go!

355
00:37:57,250 --> 00:37:58,160
Kaew.

356
00:37:58,530 --> 00:37:59,240
Let go of me.

357
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:01,440
Kaew!

358
00:38:01,750 --> 00:38:02,600
Awww.

359
00:38:02,890 --> 00:38:03,400
Come on.

360
00:38:07,100 --> 00:38:08,030
Kaew.

361
00:38:08,670 --> 00:38:09,970
Stop P’Kie.

362
00:38:10,030 --> 00:38:11,320
Stop it now.

363
00:38:11,370 --> 00:38:12,480
You're both as bad as each other.

364
00:38:12,530 --> 00:38:15,190
I regret ever trusting you.

365
00:38:16,630 --> 00:38:18,810
I shouldn't have been friends with a two-faced person like you.

366
00:38:18,860 --> 00:38:21,180
Do you think I actually wanted to be friends with someone like you, huh?

367
00:38:22,030 --> 00:38:23,530
A person like you

368
00:38:23,870 --> 00:38:27,080
has nothing good going for you besides money.

369
00:38:28,570 --> 00:38:29,880
If you were actually a good person,

370
00:38:30,150 --> 00:38:33,840
none of your wives would have betrayed you the way they do.

371
00:38:36,250 --> 00:38:37,860
Everyone who comes into your life

372
00:38:38,810 --> 00:38:41,200
is just two-faced with you anyway.

373
00:38:42,640 --> 00:38:45,340
You're just a walking ATM.

374
00:38:45,400 --> 00:38:46,210
Kaew!

375
00:38:46,460 --> 00:38:47,970
That's enough, Kaew.

376
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:49,140
Let me go.

377
00:38:50,390 --> 00:38:54,710
Someone like kie needs to know what her true nature is really like.

378
00:38:57,540 --> 00:39:01,560
No wonder... not a single person wants to be genuine with you.

379
00:39:01,940 --> 00:39:05,710
Oh... acting like some high-and-mighty princess

380
00:39:05,750 --> 00:39:07,690
who gets whatever she wants and expects everyone to bend to you, huh?

381
00:39:07,720 --> 00:39:08,480
Kaew!

382
00:39:08,750 --> 00:39:12,380
Do you have any idea how sick and tired everyone is of you?

383
00:39:14,590 --> 00:39:16,840
Even though you never registered your marriage with anyone.

384
00:39:17,210 --> 00:39:19,930
I know that even if you wanted to,

385
00:39:19,980 --> 00:39:21,930
nobody would want to register a marriage with you anyway.

386
00:39:23,050 --> 00:39:24,260
What kind of person are you?

387
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:26,320
Anyone you marry just ends up dead.

388
00:39:27,660 --> 00:39:31,840
Is this what you call having a husband-killer destiny?

389
00:39:32,830 --> 00:39:33,940
No, wait.

390
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:37,500
It should be called a wife-devouring destiny, that's more accurate.

391
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:39,090
You are a jinx!!

392
00:39:39,150 --> 00:39:40,540
Kaew Kaew

393
00:39:42,710 --> 00:39:44,260
Aunt Ros! Aunt Ros!

394
00:39:44,300 --> 00:39:46,190
Aunt Ros! Aunt Ros!

395
00:39:47,080 --> 00:39:47,810
Aunt Ros!

396
00:39:48,680 --> 00:39:51,030
Let's call an ambulance, just to be safe.

397
00:39:51,070 --> 00:39:52,090
No need.

398
00:39:52,950 --> 00:39:54,000
I’ll call it myself.

399
00:39:54,050 --> 00:39:55,370
All of you, just go back.

400
00:39:57,990 --> 00:39:58,870
Aunt Ros,

401
00:40:02,110 --> 00:40:05,250
I told you to go back! Go!

402
00:40:05,320 --> 00:40:06,280
Let's go, Kie.

403
00:40:06,670 --> 00:40:07,870
Vodka, let's go.

404
00:40:19,870 --> 00:40:20,630
Aunt Ros!

405
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:22,930
Aunt Ros!

406
00:40:33,770 --> 00:40:34,770
Oh my god!

407
00:40:35,280 --> 00:40:37,880
Why do you bring trouble upon yourself every single day?!

408
00:40:37,930 --> 00:40:39,880
If your dad and Grandpa find out about this,

409
00:40:39,940 --> 00:40:42,820
I'm definitely going to get blamed for taking poor care of Kie.

410
00:40:43,150 --> 00:40:44,570
It’s okay, Mom.

411
00:40:44,630 --> 00:40:46,780
I’ll help clear things up with Dad for you.

412
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:48,840
Thank you, Wine.

413
00:40:49,680 --> 00:40:50,990
And... and where is Kie?

414
00:40:51,720 --> 00:40:52,730
She's right over there.

415
00:40:52,760 --> 00:40:53,810
Did you bring everything here?

416
00:40:54,060 --> 00:40:55,140
Absolutely everything.

417
00:40:55,190 --> 00:40:58,520
Everything related to Ms. Kaew and Ms. Pha are here.

418
00:41:32,220 --> 00:41:33,120
Burn it all.

419
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:34,810
Yes, Ms. Kie.

420
00:41:41,590 --> 00:41:44,720
Wow, did she really slap her right at her house?

421
00:41:45,580 --> 00:41:48,100
Yeah, she did.

422
00:41:48,150 --> 00:41:50,390
K’May told me about it right after the clinic's shareholders' meeting.

423
00:41:50,980 --> 00:41:54,540
K’May said she was so distressed she didn't know what to do.

424
00:41:54,910 --> 00:41:57,460
When I first heard it, I was shocked too.

425
00:41:58,800 --> 00:42:02,740
But from what you told me, those two have been best friends since childhood.

426
00:42:03,720 --> 00:42:04,810
It's such a shame.

427
00:42:08,100 --> 00:42:09,730
I just feel bad for Kie.

428
00:42:09,770 --> 00:42:11,680
No good deed goes unpunished with her.

429
00:42:22,510 --> 00:42:23,430
Hello?

430
00:42:25,090 --> 00:42:28,740
Hello. I'm Kie’s secretary.

431
00:42:28,790 --> 00:42:30,940
She gave me your Line contact.

432
00:42:31,010 --> 00:42:35,250
She would like to compensate you for taking her to the hospital.

433
00:42:35,740 --> 00:42:36,870
That's alright.

434
00:42:36,920 --> 00:42:38,480
I already told her it wasn't necessary.

435
00:42:39,090 --> 00:42:41,360
Oh, you really can't do that.

436
00:42:41,410 --> 00:42:48,030
She strictly instructed me that the money must be transferred to you.

437
00:42:48,750 --> 00:42:50,750
Are you okay with fifty thousand?

438
00:42:50,800 --> 00:42:51,890
I'm not okay with it.

439
00:42:51,940 --> 00:42:53,600
I won't take a single baht.

440
00:42:53,640 --> 00:42:55,130
I helped because I wanted to.

441
00:42:55,180 --> 00:42:57,660
Please tell your boss thank you very much,

442
00:42:57,860 --> 00:42:58,890
but no thanks.

443
00:42:58,950 --> 00:42:59,890
That's all, goodbye.

444
00:43:00,210 --> 00:43:02,210
Oh, don't hang up yet! Please...

445
00:43:03,370 --> 00:43:06,500
I'm begging you.

446
00:43:06,560 --> 00:43:08,880
If you don't take this money,

447
00:43:09,630 --> 00:43:11,880
I'm going to be in serious trouble.

448
00:43:12,050 --> 00:43:15,740
So please, just accept this money.

449
00:43:15,800 --> 00:43:16,850
Have some empathy.

450
00:43:16,900 --> 00:43:18,370
We're all human beings, please.

451
00:43:18,410 --> 00:43:19,880
It's a whole fifty thousand!

452
00:43:20,400 --> 00:43:23,370
I'm so sorry, but I really cannot accept this.

453
00:43:23,440 --> 00:43:25,100
I feel uncomfortable taking it.

454
00:43:27,620 --> 00:43:29,010
What's going on? Who’s that?

455
00:43:30,640 --> 00:43:32,640
Just some nonsense from someone who is self-centered.

456
00:43:34,280 --> 00:43:37,560
Though, even if she is self-centered, at least she’s fair

457
00:43:38,090 --> 00:43:39,230
and straightforward.

458
00:43:39,490 --> 00:43:41,250
Hey... this kid.

459
00:43:44,900 --> 00:43:47,860
Oh my... Whose kid is this?

460
00:43:48,130 --> 00:43:49,090
Are they that rich?

461
00:43:49,140 --> 00:43:50,160
If it were me,

462
00:43:50,200 --> 00:43:52,280
a thousand baht would be okay!

463
00:43:58,080 --> 00:43:59,060
K’Kie?

464
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:06,480
Yes, K’Kie.

465
00:44:06,810 --> 00:44:07,860
Hello, Nuan.

466
00:44:08,630 --> 00:44:10,630
Has she accepted the money yet?

467
00:44:14,320 --> 00:44:16,320
I'm so sorry, K’Kie.

468
00:44:16,380 --> 00:44:18,100
I tried my best,

469
00:44:18,140 --> 00:44:20,900
but the other side just keeps refusing.

470
00:44:20,950 --> 00:44:24,150
Nuan, why can't you even handle a simple thing like this?

471
00:44:24,830 --> 00:44:26,830
Go make her take the money, no matter what.

472
00:44:28,120 --> 00:44:31,170
Otherwise, I'm going to dock your salary.

473
00:44:37,680 --> 00:44:39,680
Oh, hanging up again!

474
00:44:41,650 --> 00:44:44,480
And if she refuses the money, what on earth does that have to do with me anyway?

475
00:44:45,020 --> 00:44:48,290
Wow... Nuan’s life is just awesome.

476
00:44:51,740 --> 00:44:54,940
Alright, every problem always has me to solve it.

477
00:45:00,100 --> 00:45:02,210
Even though you never registered your marriage with anyone.

478
00:45:02,690 --> 00:45:05,430
I know that even if you wanted to,

479
00:45:05,470 --> 00:45:07,430
nobody would want to register a marriage with you anyway.

480
00:45:08,570 --> 00:45:11,860
What kind of person are you? Anyone you marry just ends up dead.

481
00:45:12,760 --> 00:45:15,760
It should be called a wife-devouring destiny, that's more accurate.

482
00:45:16,180 --> 00:45:17,220
You are a jinx!!

483
00:45:41,620 --> 00:45:42,990
Was I fired?

484
00:45:44,230 --> 00:45:46,990
But I’ve always done a great job!

485
00:45:47,270 --> 00:45:49,270
I even traveled out of town for work

486
00:45:49,850 --> 00:45:51,340
and my performance has been solid.

487
00:45:51,670 --> 00:45:52,990
Why…

488
00:45:54,220 --> 00:45:56,410
I know, but it was necessary.

489
00:45:56,980 --> 00:45:58,440
The higher-ups gave the order.

490
00:45:59,140 --> 00:46:01,140
Given the way you behaved toward K’Pijika,

491
00:46:01,410 --> 00:46:03,110
we simply cannot keep you on.

492
00:46:06,380 --> 00:46:07,480
Oh, I see.

493
00:46:11,180 --> 00:46:12,860
So it was Kie's doing, right?

494
00:46:13,840 --> 00:46:16,980
You have to understand that we are a subsidiary under their group.

495
00:46:17,330 --> 00:46:18,980
When they give an order, I have to follow it.

496
00:46:20,230 --> 00:46:21,480
I'm truly sorry.

497
00:46:43,930 --> 00:46:45,670
Did Mom actually fire her?

498
00:46:46,110 --> 00:46:48,280
Kie was the one who brought her in to work here,

499
00:46:48,320 --> 00:46:50,400
but yet she could still do this to Kie.

500
00:46:50,660 --> 00:46:51,700
Why should we keep her around?

501
00:46:52,840 --> 00:46:56,440
But Mom, Kaew is a good worker,

502
00:46:56,810 --> 00:46:58,650
and she didn't break any rules.

503
00:46:59,280 --> 00:47:00,570
What do you mean didn't break any rules?

504
00:47:00,640 --> 00:47:02,280
If she could do that to a friend,

505
00:47:02,330 --> 00:47:04,590
what's left for the organization?

506
00:47:08,260 --> 00:47:11,860
And... does Kie know about this?

507
00:47:12,870 --> 00:47:13,850
No need for her to know.

508
00:47:14,440 --> 00:47:16,720
It's best to let her rest and clear her down in Hua Hin.

509
00:47:32,450 --> 00:47:33,580
I can't believe it.

510
00:47:33,610 --> 00:47:35,650
Even the star employee got ousted.

511
00:47:36,600 --> 00:47:38,510
I heard they had some kind of fallout with K’Kie.

512
00:47:38,790 --> 00:47:41,380
Seriously? Best friends turning on each other?

513
00:47:41,420 --> 00:47:42,810
That's so intense!

514
00:47:44,370 --> 00:47:46,960
But who knows how it went down,

515
00:47:47,010 --> 00:47:48,670
it must've been pretty intense though.

516
00:47:48,890 --> 00:47:51,150
To get suddenly ousted like that out of nowhere,

517
00:47:51,190 --> 00:47:53,930
the situation definitely had to be serious, girl.

518
00:47:53,960 --> 00:47:55,380
Right? Exactly.

519
00:48:07,220 --> 00:48:08,060
Damn it.

520
00:48:47,880 --> 00:48:48,720
Excuse me!

521
00:49:18,230 --> 00:49:18,930
Here you go.

522
00:49:32,720 --> 00:49:34,400
Thank you truly, I really appreciate it.

523
00:49:34,940 --> 00:49:38,620
If you hadn't helped me, I would've been in a huge mess.

524
00:49:40,980 --> 00:49:42,180
It's no trouble at all.

525
00:49:43,100 --> 00:49:45,020
But when I went to catch you earlier,

526
00:49:45,060 --> 00:49:46,570
your body felt burning hot.

527
00:49:47,230 --> 00:49:48,700
You should go see a doctor,

528
00:49:48,750 --> 00:49:49,840
just in case it's heatstroke.

529
00:49:51,680 --> 00:49:54,400
Oh, it's completely fine.

530
00:49:55,480 --> 00:49:57,910
I guess I was just a bit stressed.

531
00:50:01,600 --> 00:50:03,320
I suddenly lost my job,

532
00:50:06,860 --> 00:50:10,780
and my girlfriend just passed away.

533
00:50:52,450 --> 00:50:53,830
Thank you though.

534
00:50:57,410 --> 00:51:02,650
But come to think of it, I was feeling burnt out here anyway.

535
00:51:04,850 --> 00:51:06,320
Getting fired is actually a good thing,

536
00:51:08,110 --> 00:51:12,950
it might be a sign for me to start fresh.

537
00:51:21,220 --> 00:51:24,960
Besides, the only reason I got to work here was

538
00:51:25,880 --> 00:51:27,880
because a toxic friend pulled strings for me.

539
00:51:30,360 --> 00:51:31,680
A toxic friend?

540
00:51:34,770 --> 00:51:35,700
Yes,

541
00:51:36,740 --> 00:51:38,330
she stole my girlfriend.

542
00:51:39,590 --> 00:51:43,850
It's a good thing that a toxic friend like that is out of my life.

